 "text": "Hi, how have you been? It depends how fluent you are speaking it yourself. If you speak it naturally, the easier it is for others. It shares so many words and patterns with English, it' like a big shared backyard. It is nice. Now go practice, so you sound as fluent as possible. The Dutch sound can be tough on English tongues, especially the g sound that English speakers usually glide over. That's a bit like asking which mountain range has more peaks. It depends completely on what you're interested in. Then go for it. It' a beautiful language that few people speak, so you' stand out without trying. Which do you think you'll enjoy more, watching Norwegian",
